LICENSING OVERVIEW (dual license)

This repository is dual-licensed by component. The authors apply these licenses to
the extent they hold the rights; see the conditions below.

  CODE                  -> MIT (see LICENSE-MIT)
    code/*.py  (the pipeline and the re-analysis / verification scripts)

  DOCS, CONSTRAINT LISTS, EVIDENCE ARRAYS  -> CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0)
    README.md, REPRODUCIBILITY.md, evidence/README.md
    protocol/*.json and code/register_extract.json  (constraint lists / register)
    evidence/arrays/**  (confirmatory + corrected arm-B arrays)

Why CC BY 4.0 for the non-code materials: the same confirmatory and corrected arm-B
arrays are already deposited, irrevocably, under CC BY 4.0 on Zenodo (results record,
DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24227377). This repository matches that verified deposit license so
the same files are not offered under two different licenses. (The Zenodo record's license
was verified from the record page: "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International".)

NOT LICENSED HERE (under either license):
  - The CIC-IDS2017 (Canadian Institute for Cybersecurity) and UNSW-NB15 (UNSW
    Canberra) raw datasets — property of their providers, under their own terms;
    not redistributed here.
  - Any third-party libraries or components, which keep their own licenses.

CONDITIONS / OPEN POINTS (read before publishing):
  1. The evidence arrays are DERIVED from CIC-IDS2017 and UNSW-NB15. The authors are
     responsible for ensuring those datasets' terms permit licensing/redistribution of
     these derived arrays — as they already asserted by depositing them under CC BY 4.0 on
     Zenodo. Excluding the raw data does not by itself settle derivative rights.
  2. The prior Zenodo deposit (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.24227377, CC BY 4.0) stands on its own;
     CC licenses are irrevocable, so this repository does not and cannot revoke or replace
     it — it is aligned with it.
  3. Publication approval: the submitting author confirms that both supervisors have approved
     publication of this repository. This approval concerns publication and the licensing choice
     recorded here; it does NOT by itself establish redistribution rights over third-party or
     dataset-derived materials, which remain governed by Conditions 1-2 above.

